# Build context exclusions for the fleet image (U1 step 6).
#
# Two jobs. The first is a smaller, faster build. The second matters more: the
# repo is public from commit one and the working tree will reference credentials
# that unlock a real mailbox, so anything credential-shaped is kept out of the
# image as well as out of git. An image layer is as durable as a commit and
# harder to notice.

# Version control and CI
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.gitleaks.toml

# Installed locally; the image installs its own from the lockfile
node_modules

# Build and test output
dist
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo

# Not needed at runtime. `*.md` matches one path segment, so this is the
# top-level prose only — src/README.md rides along with the source and is
# small enough not to be worth a second rule.
docs
test
scripts
*.md

# Credentials and local configuration. The controls are GitHub push protection
# and the gitleaks CI job (U1 step 5); this list is defence in depth, not the
# control.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
.dev.vars
.wrangler

# Deployment configuration is read by wrangler on the host, not by the container
wrangler.toml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# OS and editor
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea
.vscode
.claude
